  "minimum_safe_summary": "This narrative review explores the intricate relationship between architectural space and human psychological feelings. It posits that various architectural elements, including building type, spatial configuration, form, size, color, and texture, can evoke diverse psychological responses such as relaxation, esteem, spaciousness, crowdedness, security, comfort, affinity, and distance. The paper highlights how individual differences and prior experiences modulate these feelings, and emphasizes the importance of considering psychological impacts in architectural design to create harmonious and artistic spaces. No specific limitations of the review itself are explicitly stated, but the complexity of the human-building relationship is acknowledged.",
